[background arg="res://assets/backgrounds/Therapy room.png" fade="0.0"]
set {flags.met_kamila} = true
audio mbg1 "res://assets/audio/ElevenLabs_Cosy_therapist_office,_ full.mp3"
audio mbg2 "res://assets/audio/Silent clock ticking.mp3" [volume="0.0"]
join bea rightmost [mirrored="true"]
bea: There is a woman in the waiting room who is, at this precise moment, doing yoga against the bookshelf.
bea: I know that sounds manageable. It isn't. She reorganized your psychology shelf during the split. Two minutes. I checked the system she used — I think it's personal.
player: [i]Of course.[/i]
bea: She looked at me once. My pen resigned. Not fell — resigned. I have to respect that kind of authority.
bea: I've established a warning protocol. One knock means tea. Two means I've tripped over something again. Three means she's critiquing my posture and I need immediate emotional reinforcement. You're going to be brilliant. I'm going to go have a small quiet crisis. Goodbye.
leave bea
narrator: The door opens. She enters the way weather enters a room — not dramatically, just inevitably.
join kamila (Embarrassment_Animated) leftmost
kamila (Embarrassment_Animated): Stark. And this desk is performing poverty.
narrator: She draws a fingernail along the wood. Not aggressive. The way you test a bruise — to see how deep it goes.
kamila (Disapproval): Cheap veneer. You want to look established. It almost works.
player: Welcome, Ms. Vance. I'm Dr. Cole.
kamila (Amusement): I know who you are. The question is whether you do.
narrator: She stops three paces from your chair and studies you with the unhurried interest of someone who has all the time in the world and has made sure of it.
kamila (Curiosity): Your breathing is wrong. Two centimeters too high. You're bracing against something that hasn't happened yet.
narrator: She is annoyingly, precisely correct about this.
# CH_KAM_S1_01 | OPT_01=Clinical [composure:easy]  OPT_02=Adaptive [default]  OPT_03=Razor [nerve:medium]
- "The work here is on internal architecture, not furniture. And I prefer professional titles until we've earned something else, Ms. Vance." | [dice="composure:easy" win="Path_Clinical_Intro" lose="Fail_Opening_Clinical"]
- "I'm still finding the room's character. Help yourself to whatever geometry suits you."
	set {flags.kamila.CH_KAM_S1_01} = "OPT_KAM_S1_01_02"
	jump Path_Adaptive_Intro
- "Thirty seconds in. You've audited the furniture, rearranged my shelf, and diagnosed my breathing. Is this how you arrive everywhere, or is there something specific about therapists?" | [dice="nerve:medium" win="Path_Razor_Intro" lose="Fail_Opening_Razor"]

label Path_Clinical_Intro
set {flags.kamila.CH_KAM_S1_01} = "OPT_KAM_S1_01_01"
do PatientManager.add_therapy("kamila", 4)
do PatientManager.add_bond("kamila", -2)
narrator: She considers the sentence. Then him. A bird reconsidering a worm.
kamila (Amusement): "Internal architecture." A fence.
kamila (Approval): Fine. Fences tell me everything about what's on both sides. I find them useful.
narrator: She drops onto the couch with the ease of someone returning to a familiar seat — not sitting, exactly. Claiming.
kamila (Amusement): You be the doctor. I'll be the patient. Let's see who's better at it.
jump Merge_After_Intro

label Fail_Opening_Clinical
do PatientManager.add_therapy("kamila", -2)
do PatientManager.add_bond("kamila", 2)
narrator: The sentence arrives with the right words in the wrong order of conviction. She notes it without mercy.
kamila (Amusement): "Internal architecture." The emphasis is wrong. It should land on "architecture," not "internal."
narrator: She settles on the couch. Proprietary. Inevitable.
kamila (Curiosity): Better than nothing. The previous doctor opened with a handshake that lasted four seconds. You're already ahead.
jump Merge_After_Intro

label Path_Adaptive_Intro
do PatientManager.add_therapy("kamila", 1)
do PatientManager.add_bond("kamila", 2)
kamila (Curiosity): "The room's character." You're nervous and dressing it as philosophy.
narrator: She doesn't sit. She drapes herself across the back of the couch — elbows on the cushion top, studying him from a position that is technically lower but somehow isn't.
kamila (Pride): Most people walk into a strange room and immediately claim a corner. You offered yours. That's either generous or weak. I haven't decided which.
player: What would you prefer?
narrator: A small pause. Something arrived that she didn't expect.
kamila (Curiosity): Nobody's asked me that before.
jump Merge_After_Intro

label Path_Razor_Intro
set {flags.kamila.CH_KAM_S1_01} = "OPT_KAM_S1_01_03"
do PatientManager.add_therapy("kamila", -2)
do PatientManager.add_bond("kamila", 5)
narrator: A short exhale — involuntary, immediately controlled. She halts two steps past the desk.
kamila (Realization): Thirty seconds and you're counting.
player: Patterns. Hard not to see them when they're this clean.
kamila (Desire): Most new doctors spend the first session establishing that I'm complicated. You're skipping straight to the interesting part.
kamila (Desire): That's either experience or desperation. I'm curious which.
[photo_opportunity id="kamila_desk_lean" patient="kamila" title="The Predatory Stance" description="Kamila testing the boundaries of the desk, the professional distance somewhere on the floor between them." portrait="res://assets/photos/kamila/kamila_desk_lean.png"]
jump Merge_After_Intro

label Fail_Opening_Razor
do PatientManager.add_therapy("kamila", -3)
do PatientManager.add_bond("kamila", 3)
narrator: Aimed correctly. Announced too loudly.
kamila (Amusement): "Is this how you arrive everywhere." There was a question mark in there you were trying to hide. I heard it anyway.
narrator: She drops onto the couch, victorious, unhurried.
kamila (Curiosity): Next time — don't let me see you wind up. The surprise is the only part that matters.
jump Merge_After_Intro

label Merge_After_Intro
narrator: Kamila settles into the couch — not comfortable, exactly. Occupied. The way a general occupies a position she intends to keep.
kamila (Neutral): Right. Paperwork. What do you need to know.
player: Your intake form. Insomnia, psychosomatic tension. For someone who teaches structural wellness, that has a certain irony.
kamila (Disgust): "Wellness." A surrender dressed as an aspiration.
kamila (Pride): My students come to me wanting to feel better. I'm not interested in feelings. I'm interested in results. Pain that improves you and pain that destroys you are entirely different things. Most people spend their lives not learning the distinction. Most instructors don't teach it because they never learned it themselves.
player: And you go home and can't sleep.
kamila (Anger): I lie in the dark at two in the morning with nothing left to push against. The world goes soft. I want to break something just to hear it break.
narrator: Her gaze drifts — past him, toward the locked door. A private geography. She doesn't seem to know she mapped it.
kamila (Neutral): You moved the bookshelf. It used to be against the east wall.
player: [i]First appointment. She knows where the bookshelf used to be.[/i]
# CH_KAM_S1_PREV | OPT_01=Asked [default]  OPT_02=Filed [default]
- "You've been in this office before."
	set {flags.kamila.CH_KAM_S1_PREV} = "OPT_KAM_S1_PREV_01"
	narrator: A small smile. The kind that arrived already finished.
	kamila (Amusement): Previous doctor. This office. We had a productive arrangement.
	kamila (Neutral): Until he decided to stop.
	player: "Decided."
	kamila (Neutral): His word.
	player: [i]Not hers. Interesting.[/i]
	[add_note patient="kamila" note="K. Vance. Yoga instructor. Chronic insomnia. Psychosomatic left-shoulder tension. Knew the bookshelf's previous position without prompting. Was a patient under the previous doctor — this office. 'Productive arrangement,' her words. He 'decided' to stop — his word, not hers. She's been in this chair before. She knows it. She knows I know it."]
- [File it. Don't ask yet.]
	set {flags.kamila.CH_KAM_S1_PREV} = "OPT_KAM_S1_PREV_02"
	player: [i]She dropped that like a key on the floor to see if I'd pick it up. I left it. The shape of it is more useful unasked.[/i]
	[add_note patient="kamila" note="K. Vance. Yoga instructor. Chronic insomnia. Psychosomatic left-shoulder tension. Knew the bookshelf's previous position without prompting. This office means something to her. She's been in this chair before — I'd stake the license on it. She dropped it and walked away. I left it on the floor. Next time."]
narrator: She stands without announcement. Crosses to the desk. Stops eighteen inches away.
narrator: Eighteen inches is inside conversational distance. She is aware of the number.
kamila (Pride): Left shoulder. Tell me what you see. Not the chart — me.
player: [i]She smells of sandalwood and something that might be a dare. The left shoulder rides four degrees higher than the right — a chronic pattern, not acute. There's a story in that shoulder that predates the studio by years. The question is whether she wants me to read it or merely to prove I can.[/i]
# CH_KAM_S1_02 | OPT_01=Spasm [perception:medium]  OPT_02=Order [composure:easy]  OPT_03=Tension [nerve:medium]
- "Your trapezius is locked — hyper-tonic spasm, levator too. That's not a posture problem. That's a siege." | [dice="perception:medium" win="Path_Observe_Spasm" lose="Fail_Standoff_Spasm"]
- "Step back from my desk, Kamila. I can't assess a somatic symptom while you're conducting a dominance experiment." | [dice="composure:easy" win="Path_Order_Back" lose="Fail_Standoff_Order"]
- "I see someone holding her breath to see what I do with the next three seconds." | [dice="nerve:medium" win="Path_Trace_Tension" lose="Fail_Standoff_Tension"]

label Fail_Standoff_Spasm
narrator: The diagnosis is there, somewhere in the clinical fog — and then it isn't. She watches with the patience of someone who expected this.
kamila (Amusement): Close. Come back next week with your anatomy. I enjoyed the attempt.
do PatientManager.add_therapy("kamila", -2)
do PatientManager.add_bond("kamila", 1)
jump Merge_After_Standoff

label Fail_Standoff_Order
narrator: "Step back—" with a question mark buried inside it. She hears it.
kamila (Amusement): You asked. That's what you didn't mean to do.
narrator: She takes one more step before — entirely on her own timeline — retreating to the couch.
kamila (Neutral): Let me know when you figure out how to do that again. The first version was interesting.
do PatientManager.add_therapy("kamila", -2)
do PatientManager.add_bond("kamila", 1)
jump Merge_After_Standoff

label Fail_Standoff_Tension
narrator: He aims for it. Pulls back at the last second. She catalogs this with genuine professional interest.
kamila (Amusement): You had something. You chose not to throw it.
kamila (Curiosity): Some locked doors stay shut longest because of the secrets on the visitor's side.
do PatientManager.add_therapy("kamila", -1)
do PatientManager.add_bond("kamila", 2)
jump Merge_After_Standoff

label Path_Observe_Spasm
set {flags.kamila.CH_KAM_S1_02} = "OPT_KAM_S1_02_01"
do PatientManager.add_therapy("kamila", 4)
do PatientManager.add_bond("kamila", 1)
narrator: She freezes. Then something shifts — not softness. Recognition. Being correctly read is its own intimacy.
kamila (Realization): Trapezius and levator. Yes.
kamila (Remorse): Three years of breathing into it, meditating around it, adjusting half a thousand other bodies while carrying it. It won't release. My own skeleton staging a quiet mutiny.
player: Because you're treating it like occupied territory. It doesn't need conquest — it needs a negotiated peace.
kamila (Realization): What a civilized way to describe a war I'm already losing.
jump Merge_After_Standoff

label Path_Order_Back
set {flags.kamila.CH_KAM_S1_02} = "OPT_KAM_S1_02_02"
do PatientManager.add_therapy("kamila", 5)
do PatientManager.add_bond("kamila", -2)
narrator: She stops. A flicker of genuine surprise — real enough she doesn't catch it in time.
kamila (Surprise): You said that like it was going to work.
player: I did.
narrator: She returns to the couch. Her choice, her timeline — but she returns.
kamila (Approval): That's the first true thing you've said since I walked in.
jump Merge_After_Standoff

label Path_Trace_Tension
set {flags.kamila.CH_KAM_S1_02} = "OPT_KAM_S1_02_03"
do PatientManager.add_therapy("kamila", -3)
do PatientManager.add_bond("kamila", 6)
narrator: Something changes in the room. The specific weight of being observed back.
kamila (Desire): And what do you do with those three seconds?
player: Watch you not breathe.
narrator: She lets the breath out. Slow. Deliberate. Like she chose to.
kamila (Amusement): Most doctors pretend not to see things. Professional courtesy. You're going to be a problem.
jump Merge_After_Standoff

label Merge_After_Standoff
if {flags.kamila.CH_KAM_S1_02} == "OPT_KAM_S1_02_02":
	narrator: Kamila sits properly on the couch for the first time — like she's accepted the room on its own terms, temporarily.
else:
	narrator: She returns to the couch, bringing her geometry with her.
- "The Tyranny of Perfect Geometry" | [if {discoveries.kamila_tyranny_geometry} != true] [else="hide" disco="kamila_tyranny_geometry"]
- "The Somatic Control Mechanism" | [if {discoveries.kamila_somatic_control} != true] [else="hide" disco="kamila_somatic_control"]
- Skip it
player: Your students. The ones who exhaust you — tell me what actually happens in that room.
kamila (Disgust): They arrive broken and want me to make them comfortable with it. I don't do comfortable. I fix what's broken.
kamila (Pride): I push until the performance stops — until something fundamental gives and they find out what they actually are underneath all of it. Raw. Furious. Embarrassed. Real. Some cry. Most come back. All of them leave different.
player: And then you go home and can't sleep.
kamila (Anger): I lie in the dark with nothing left to push against. The world goes soft and I want to break something just to hear it break.
player: You're describing the same problem you cure in others.
# CH_KAM_S1_03 | OPT_01=Deconstruction [intellect:medium]  OPT_02=Diagnostic [knowledge:easy]  OPT_03=Seductive [nerve:medium]
- "You're not burning out. You're in withdrawal. The studio is the only place your real self is allowed to exist. The insomnia is everything else asking where she went." | [dice="intellect:medium" win="Path_Deconstruction" lose="Fail_Deconstruction"]
- "Classic compensatory displacement — when the large things resist control, the small ones get colonized. Your students aren't students. They're safe targets." | [dice="knowledge:easy" win="Path_Diagnostic" lose="Fail_Diagnostic"]
- "You've spent years perfecting dominance because no one has ever pushed back. You don't need more control, Kamila. You need to lose it. Just once. Properly." | [dice="nerve:medium" win="Path_Seductive_Insight" lose="Fail_Seductive_Insight"]

label Path_Deconstruction
set {flags.kamila.CH_KAM_S1_03} = "OPT_KAM_S1_03_01"
do PatientManager.add_therapy("kamila", 6)
do PatientManager.add_bond("kamila", -1)
kamila (Anger): "Real self." You're implying there's a version of me that's performing.
player: Isn't there?
narrator: She doesn't answer. That is the answer.
kamila (Amusement): Terrible bedside manner. Unexpectedly useful.
jump Merge_After_Analysis

label Fail_Deconstruction
do PatientManager.add_therapy("kamila", -2)
do PatientManager.add_bond("kamila", 1)
narrator: Accurate. Delivered without the conviction that would make it land. She hears the textbook behind it.
kamila (Disapproval): You've recognized the pattern. That's not the same as understanding it.
kamila (Amusement): Next week — say it like it costs you something. Not like you're handing in an assignment.
jump Merge_After_Analysis

label Path_Diagnostic
set {flags.kamila.CH_KAM_S1_03} = "OPT_KAM_S1_03_02"
do PatientManager.add_therapy("kamila", 4)
narrator: She sighs — not boredom, exactly. Something closer to the sound of a door opening slightly.
kamila (Disgust): Compensatory displacement. God, you're going to explain me to myself with vocabulary.
player: Would you prefer I was wrong?
kamila (Anger): I'd prefer something that costs you something. Your jargon is accurate and safe. Name the cage before you count the bars.
kamila (Remorse): But yes. The physics are right. I can't control anything large, so I make the small things absolute. It just... isn't working anymore.
narrator: Something in her voice, for just a moment, that isn't armor.
jump Merge_After_Analysis

label Fail_Diagnostic
do PatientManager.add_therapy("kamila", -3)
do PatientManager.add_bond("kamila", 1)
narrator: She sits forward the instant the jargon lands. He's handed her the perfect structure to demolish and she begins immediately.
kamila (Anger): You're using an encyclopedia to explain a hurricane.
kamila (Disapproval): I've read every book you're drawing from. I read them in this office, actually.
narrator: She lets that sit there. Watches him take inventory.
kamila (Pride): The previous doctor had better vocabulary. He also missed. But at least he aimed somewhere interesting.
jump Merge_After_Analysis

label Fail_Seductive_Insight
do PatientManager.add_therapy("kamila", -2)
do PatientManager.add_bond("kamila", 2)
narrator: You had it — perfectly aimed — and pulled back at the last second. She watches the retreat with genuine interest.
kamila (Amusement): You saw something. Then chose not to say it.
kamila (Curiosity): What scared you more — the diagnosis, or what it would make us?
jump Merge_After_Analysis

label Path_Seductive_Insight
set {flags.kamila.CH_KAM_S1_03} = "OPT_KAM_S1_03_03"
do PatientManager.add_therapy("kamila", -4)
do PatientManager.add_bond("kamila", 7)
narrator: She goes very still.
narrator: Not the controlled stillness she deploys in the studio. The other kind — the kind that arrives just before impact.
kamila (Desire): "Lose it. Properly."
narrator: She says it the way you test ice with your foot — gently, with your weight behind it, gauging whether it holds.
narrator: Her hands fall still in her lap. She looks at them for exactly one second. In that second, nobody is performing.
[photo_opportunity id="kamila_unguarded" patient="kamila" title="The Unguarded Moment" description="Kamila, for exactly one second, forgetting to be Kamila." portrait="res://assets/photos/kamila/kamila_unguarded.png"]
if {flags.last_photo_success}:
	do PatientManager.add_therapy("kamila", 3)
	do PatientManager.add_bond("kamila", 2)
kamila (Desire): That's a very stupid thing to say to a woman who broke her last therapist, {game.player_first}.
player: What happened to him?
narrator: A beat.
kamila (Amusement): He stopped practicing.
narrator: She lets it sit.
kamila: Abruptly.
jump Merge_After_Analysis

label Merge_After_Analysis
narrator: Kamila glances at the clock. Something in her expression that might, charitably, be called disappointment.
kamila (Neutral): Fifty minutes.
kamila (Curiosity): You don't have the weight of this office yet, {game.player_first}. The person who sat in that chair before you was embedded in it. You feel like you arrived from somewhere else entirely and haven't decided if you're staying.
player: I'm staying.
kamila (Amusement): You keep saying things like that. I notice.
# CH_KAM_S1_04 | OPT_01=Ironclad [composure:medium]  OPT_02=Intimate [nerve:easy]  OPT_03=Standard [default]
- "For homework — don't adjust a single student this week. Observe the chaos. Don't correct it. I want to know what happens to you when you're not allowed to fix anything." | [dice="composure:medium" win="Path_End_Ironclad" lose="Fail_End_Ironclad"]
- "Next time, leave the instructor at the door. I want to meet whoever's exhausted underneath." | [dice="nerve:easy" win="Path_End_Intimate" lose="Fail_End_Intimate"]
- "Same time next week. Through Beatrix, please. And perhaps less caffeine before bed."
	set {flags.kamila.CH_KAM_S1_04} = "OPT_KAM_S1_04_03"
	do PatientManager.add_therapy("kamila", 2)
	do PatientManager.add_bond("kamila", 1)
	jump Path_End_Standard

label Path_End_Ironclad
set {flags.kamila.CH_KAM_S1_04} = "OPT_KAM_S1_04_01"
do PatientManager.add_therapy("kamila", 6)
do PatientManager.add_bond("kamila", -3)
kamila (Annoyance): That's sadistic.
player: It's therapeutic.
kamila (Annoyance): Those aren't mutually exclusive.
narrator: She considers this for a genuine moment.
kamila (Neutral): Fine. Next week.
jump Final_Cliffhanger_Beat

label Fail_End_Ironclad
do PatientManager.add_therapy("kamila", -2)
do PatientManager.add_bond("kamila", 1)
narrator: The instruction arrives as a suggestion wearing a command's clothes. She notes the tailor's error immediately.
kamila (Amusement): "Let's see if you can handle it." Should have stopped at "don't correct them."
narrator: She stands, adjusts her bag.
kamila (Neutral): I'll observe without correcting. Not because you told me to — because I want to see how wrong your hypothesis is.
jump Final_Cliffhanger_Beat

label Path_End_Intimate
set {flags.kamila.CH_KAM_S1_04} = "OPT_KAM_S1_04_02"
do PatientManager.add_therapy("kamila", -2)
do PatientManager.add_bond("kamila", 6)
if {flags.kamila.CH_KAM_S1_03} == "OPT_KAM_S1_03_03":
	narrator: She's still close. She leans slightly and sets a small card on the open notebook — dark paper, text almost illegible.
else:
	narrator: She rises, crosses to the desk, places a small card on the notebook — dark paper, text almost illegible.
kamila (Desire): Whoever's underneath shows up at inconvenient times. I'll be here.
narrator: She picks up her bag. Something in how she moves toward the door — less architecture, more actual.
jump Final_Cliffhanger_Beat

label Fail_End_Intimate
do PatientManager.add_therapy("kamila", -1)
do PatientManager.add_bond("kamila", 2)
if {flags.kamila.CH_KAM_S1_03} == "OPT_KAM_S1_03_03":
	narrator: She pulls back from the desk. Something flickers — not quite disappointment. Recalibration.
else:
	narrator: She rises from the couch. Something flickers — not quite disappointment. Recalibration.
kamila (Neutral): "Exhausted underneath." That almost landed.
kamila (Amusement): Try again next week. With less announcement.
jump Final_Cliffhanger_Beat

label Path_End_Standard
if {flags.kamila.CH_KAM_S1_03} == "OPT_KAM_S1_03_03":
	narrator: She straightens, steps back from the desk, smooths her outfit.
else:
	narrator: She stands, smooths her outfit.
kamila (Disgust): Caffeine isn't the problem. The problem is my brain hasn't agreed to stop for four years.
kamila (Amusement): Try not to let the session occupy you too long tonight, {game.player_formal}. You look like you need the rest far more than I do.
jump Final_Cliffhanger_Beat

label Final_Cliffhanger_Beat
narrator: She walks toward the door without hurrying. People who've already won don't hurry.
narrator: Her hand finds the handle. She stops.
narrator: Her gaze moves — not to him, not to the exit — to the other door. The old one. The lock with no key in any drawer he's opened.
narrator: She looks at it the way you look at something that remembers you.
update kamila (Neutral)
kamila: That door.
player: [i]Not a question. Not an accusation. Its name.[/i]
# CH_KAM_S1_DOOR | OPT_01=Lied [default]  OPT_02=Silent [default]
- "That's storage."
	set {flags.kamila.CH_KAM_S1_DOOR} = "OPT_KAM_S1_DOOR_01"
	kamila (Amusement): Mm.
- [Say nothing. Watch where she looks.]
	set {flags.kamila.CH_KAM_S1_DOOR} = "OPT_KAM_S1_DOOR_02"
	player: [i]She holds the look for one beat longer than curiosity would require. Then she looks at me. She knows I noticed.[/i]
kamila (Neutral): You haven't tried it yet.
narrator: She leaves. The door shuts with a click that sounds like a period at the end of a sentence that started somewhere else entirely.
leave kamila
join bea rightmost [mirrored="true"]
narrator: Bea materializes with coffee. She is looking at the wall above the locked door — specifically not at it.
bea: She's going to be a lot, isn't she.
narrator: She doesn't wait for an answer.
leave bea
if {flags.kamila.CH_KAM_S1_03} == "OPT_KAM_S1_03_03":
	[add_note patient="kamila" note="K.V. — 'He stopped practicing.' Pause. 'Abruptly.' She split it in two deliberately. The space between those words is where the whole confession lives. She knows exactly what she is. She's testing whether I do too. The insomnia isn't control withdrawal — it's what happens when you can't outrun yourself."]
else:
	[add_note patient="kamila" note="K.V. — control as armor, not ambition. The insomnia is the body refusing to stay conquered. The shoulder won't release because the mind won't allow it. Whatever she's defending against stopped being external a long time ago. She's at war with herself now. The question is whether she knows it."]
do PatientManager.mark_session_done("kamila")
jump between_patients/